    (ROOT / 'RESULTS.md').write_text("The X81 makes it possible to test whether a defined query is already determined within its decision uncertainty and to calculate how few observations are needed in a declared sampling model. Reference is published Catphan images, laser group data, screw preload, coping gap and break loads. All 17 numeric gap and 30 measurement groups/ 51 physical edges are available in [gaptable](GAP_DECISION_TABLE.md). No full physical or clinical decisions are certified.\n\n| Question | What Is Determined/Build | Resolution |\n|---|---|---|\n| CBCT : more precision? | Three repetitions leave 134 – 142HU_ref error. Baselinevalt AIR + LDPE +Teflon provides 180.318 HU_ref holding errors; 40HU_ref - gate fails . | PER_SURFACE_REGION |\n| Laser: vilka gruppkontraster syns redan? |4 / 9 simultaneous 95% without operation, 2 / 9 with 0.40° C contrast budget. Conditional n 4 ; no individual warranty. | POPULATION |\n| Laser: minsta projicerade provplan? |139 versus 450 specimen when allocating evenly for the same 9 contrast target, 3.24 × less. En0.26 ° C contrast is under 0.41° C irreducible budget; no repeats are enough. | PHENOMENOLOGICAL plan from POPULATION SD |\n| Screw : visible preload reduction? |76.2 N; 95% worst covariance[47.264,105.136 ] N at 25 paired specimen . Replicated sign question needs projected 6 pairs with this SD . | POPULATION |\n| PDL : enough point accuracy? |0.65 +0.60 N digitization budget< 1.66068 N frozen discrete tolerance. Inaction, rate and physical material transfer persist. | POPULATION |\n| Crime load: survives published funds its sampling uncertainty? |One of the three empirical mean gates is completed, two becomes UNRESOLVED. Two additional goal is Weibull Closure Agent with unknown covariance. | POPULATION |\n| Replica→CT-korrigering? |60.82 μm Amann MO contrast provides simultaneous worst-covarian interval[-19.95,141.59 ] µm. Projicerat15 pairs resolve the sign issue under the same SD; method/ state remains confused. | POPULATION ; regional consumer |\n\nCBCT data comes from [RadRepro v 1 ](https://zenodo.org/records/15207526), not dental HA or bone mechanics. The temperature comes from [Geraldo-Martins2005 ](https://doi.org/10.1089/pho.2005.23.182), Table2's 184 ; ± 0.1° C instrument accuracy is indicated on the same page. n 4 is still a balancing inference, not explicitly verified cell count. Preloadfacit is [Sagheb2023 ](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1186/s40729-023-00473-3), Table1 /Results. The Replica table is [Cunali2017 ](https://doi.org/10.1590/0103-6440201601531), Table1's 470 . The criminal agents are [Chen2024 ](https://doi.org/10.3390/ma17020365), Table2 . The primary tables and 24 raw ROI medians are recalculated independently; rawarrayhashar are available in results.json.\n\nA little residual doesn't mean a decision is safe. The swarm's claim that 94% of the laser proxy error is sensor noise is not identified: its 0.71° C SD comes from another preparation regimen and mixes specimen/process/sensor. MAE has no additive variance identity. The browsing was done after R1 : s own calculation; the instrument accuracy of the laser paper changed the next design to an explicit operating budget test. No source interpretation replaced table facit.\n\nAdequateness test 1 holds MAE and maximum residual exactly equal ( identity error 0 ) but alters two's localized decisions. The smallest extension is signed error intervals at the right site / state . Specimen 2 holds margin agents, SD and mean difference exactly equal (identity error 0 ), but a paired 95% interval changes from positive to threshold cross. The minimum extra moment is regional parade covariance, with specimen - ID / state . Pooled Pearson over several regions in Cunali is not that covariance. Own fixture is used only for these adequacy counter-examples, never as empirical reference .\n\nThe remaining lab front is conditional. M01 is cheap shared need for 12 edges but alone measurement type for one; M11 touches 9 and is the sole type of four. Under X71 : s assumed hours are retained M01 → M02 → M04 on the same 12 pilot crowns; R3 : s two AND -ready-to-type edges are not X71 : s five D-queries . The number of real decisions that reverses per specimen and cost is UNKNOWN , so there is no empirical total ranking. All 30 groups first receive a defined contract; they are not 30 lab orders. Extra60 kroner's setup cost and full 72-plan remain UNKNOWN.\n\nThe uncertainty intervals are normal distribution/id-closure with published plug-in SD and some fixed predictions. Rigorous physical enclosure and the uncertainty of the fictitious endpoints are missing. The Varken139 test plan or 6 pair plan is an empirically validated power size, power calculation or generalization guarantee. 6 HA × position- ROI is only 4 calibration points +2 holding test under a specified bilinary contract; precision/replicit must be measured.\n\nThe check with the same information reproduces source rituals, lagrange interpolation and AND amounts. 18 actual injected errors are dropped. No algorithmic superiority claim is made. Five open non-physical edges are rejected from the lab list; 11% -like sigma or costs have not been invented. Source selection/default and all preserved failures are found in results.json and DEVIATIONS_AND_FAILURES.json.\n\n![Decision uncertainty and projected experimental plan](figures/DECISION_WITHIN_NOISE.png)\n\nRun `./run_all.sh` . It restores three designs, original data controls, error injections, table and figure without network or GPU . All new result is PENDING_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW .\n".replace('11% -like sigma or costs', 'Physical sigma or costs').replace('Primary tables and 24 raw ROI medians', 'Primary tables and 132 raw ROI medians').replace('simultant95%', 'nominellt simultant95%').replace('One of the three empirical mean gates is completed', 'Conditional balanced n 10 clears one of three mean gates').replace('sampling model with plug-in SD', 'sampling model with plug-in SD'))
    (ROOT / 'README_DEMO.md').write_text('X81 answers which existing dental questions survive their uncertainty interval and provides executable trial plans for the rest. The idea is to bring a signed, localised observation interval all the way to the decision limit of the issue. Repetitions may reduce sampling uncertainty; operation, missing information and observation bias retains their own fields.\n\nRun from any directory:\n\n```bash\n./run_all.sh\n```\n\nRequires Python3, NumPy, SciPy, Matplotlib and lxml in the existing environment. Under 1 GB for the run-through small steps, ≤ 4 threads, no GPU / network. Small inputs is saved during raw; four external ROI cache files are kept on original paths with hash. No new large arrays are created.\n\n| Results | Outcome |\n|---|---|\n| Full coverage |17 gap, 30 groups, 51 physical edges |\n| Precision solves CBCT bias? |No: 3 Repeat Agent 134 – 142HU_ref ; selected calibration error 180.318 > 40HU_ref |\n| Cooling contrast with a drift budget |2 / 9 delimited mean contrasts are determined; n 4 conditional |\n| Minimum projicerade observationer |139 against 450 for nine thermal non-operational contrasts; source SD and sampling resolution |\n| Full physical validation |0 ; remaining physics and decision thresholds UNKNOWN |\n| Felkontroller |18 / 18 rejects injected error; 24 ROI -mediar directly reread |\n\n[Gap table](GAP_DECISION_TABLE.md) contains justification per line. [RESULTS.md ](RESULTS.md) provides measurement facit and all boundaries. [Figure](figures/DECISION_WITHIN_NOISE.png) can be exported; SVG is located next door. `results.json` retains fine edge levels, contemporaneity/transfer, rawhashar and PHENOMENOLOGICAL cost debt.\n\nWhat does not holds : a residual under the group SD is not a decision proof. Published group scattering is not sensor noise; MAE cannot be deconvolved in square clocks. P95 -ytrest is not the local of truth. Releasemasker is not independent readers. Normal sample model with plug-in SD provides no rigorous physical /individual guarantees. The number of projected specimen is a simulation and minimum n within frozen design space, not a laboratory saving like been measured. Pilot12 does not replace the original 72 crown sample.\n\nData sources/rights: RadRepro v 1 [doi: 10.5281/zenodo.15207526 ](https://zenodo.org/records/15207526), CC BY4.0 ; Sagheb2023 and Chen2024 , CC BY4.0 articles; Geraldo2005 and Cunali2017 are used as local numeric table extract with DOI /page, not new dataset license. ToothFairy2 CC BY-SA4.0 , Bits2Bites CC BY-NC-SA4.0 : only already de-identified results summaries are reused. Mandible defects, Teeth3DS and MMDental are not used. No personal data. Source tables/light images are not clinical recommendations.\n\nThe next specimen is either a reference/blank channel that measures differential drift in the pulp bench or a HA × position phantom with 4 calibration ROI +2 holding test under an explicit bilinary model, followed by paralysed bone mechanical reference if the decision needs E. Only then does a new frozen physical predict a new measurement.\n'.replace('four external ROI cache files', '22 externa ROI-cachefiler').replace('24 ROI -mediar directly reread', '132 ROI -mediar directly reread'))
